WEBVTT

01:24.060 --> 01:29.980
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

01:31.150 --> 01:42.050
<i>I'm a high-ranking officer of the Evil League,
which fights daily to wipe out humankind</i>

01:42.050 --> 01:45.620
<i>and claim the Earth in the 
name of our home planet.</i>

01:46.280 --> 01:49.820
<i>But today is my day off.</i>

01:50.410 --> 01:52.740
<i>On the way home from the supermarket,</i>

01:52.740 --> 01:55.620
<i>I was enjoying some sun in the park</i>

01:55.910 --> 01:58.900
<i>while sorting through my panda photos.</i>

02:01.820 --> 02:06.020
I'm telling you, this'll be another year
Orihime and Hikoboshi fail to meet.

02:06.020 --> 02:08.860
What?! They will <i>too</i> meet!

02:09.170 --> 02:12.290
<i>Orihime? Hikoboshi?</i>

02:12.290 --> 02:14.240
<i>Who the heck are they?</i>

02:15.150 --> 02:19.830
<i>I can't help but get caught up in this 
conversation the children are having.</i>

02:20.230 --> 02:23.540
They totally won't. I mean, it always rains.

02:25.230 --> 02:27.500
<i>If it rains, they can't meet?</i>

02:27.840 --> 02:30.830
It might be clear this year!

02:30.830 --> 02:33.810
The forecast is calling 
for rain on the seventh.

02:35.320 --> 02:37.630
<i>They're only concerned about the seventh?</i>

02:38.010 --> 02:44.010
<i>That must mean Orihime and Hikoboshi 
have plans to go out that day,</i>

02:44.380 --> 02:47.520
<i>but it keeps getting rained out every year.</i>

02:48.080 --> 02:50.810
<i>They should consider a different date.</i>

02:50.810 --> 02:53.910
<i>Is that the only day they can make it work?</i>

02:53.910 --> 02:58.400
It's because they spent all their 
time having fun, not working.

02:58.400 --> 02:59.880
They got what they deserve.

03:00.850 --> 03:03.370
Just like my mom and dad.

03:05.740 --> 03:07.390
Hibiki...

03:07.960 --> 03:12.550
That reminds me, Hibiki,
 aren't you moving on the seventh?

03:12.550 --> 03:14.910
Yeah, I'm moving in with my grandparents.

03:14.910 --> 03:16.220
Is that far away?

03:16.220 --> 03:17.320
It is.

03:17.760 --> 03:20.330
What about your mom and dad?

03:20.330 --> 03:21.510
They're not going.

03:22.040 --> 03:24.650
I'll come see you off!

03:24.650 --> 03:26.830
You don't have to, Aya. It'll be raining.

03:27.380 --> 03:29.010
I'll come anyway!

03:29.010 --> 03:30.220
You'll get wet.

03:32.330 --> 03:33.790
I don't care!

03:34.600 --> 03:38.480
I'm not Orihime, so I can come 
see you even if it's raining!

03:39.940 --> 03:42.270
Does that make me Hikoboshi?

03:42.270 --> 03:43.830
Or it can be the other way around.

03:44.340 --> 03:46.050
Either's fine by me.

03:47.380 --> 03:50.520
I better head home or I'll get an earful.

03:51.090 --> 03:52.680
Thanks for letting me play this.

03:52.680 --> 03:56.130
Oh, you can hang on to it, Hibiki.

03:56.130 --> 03:58.730
I'll borrow my brother's, so it's fine.

03:58.730 --> 03:59.840
I can't, Aya.

03:59.840 --> 04:01.960
Somebody bought it for you, right?

04:03.340 --> 04:06.470
I'll try wishing that
someone buys me one too.

04:07.630 --> 04:09.020
Hibiki!

04:09.020 --> 04:12.450
The seventh, okay?!
 I swear I'll come see you!

04:15.520 --> 04:17.370
Bye-bye!

04:18.270 --> 04:20.400
<b>Unohara Shopping District</b>

04:22.270 --> 04:27.740
<i>I never did find out who 
Orihime and Hikoboshi are.</i>

04:27.740 --> 04:31.540
<i>But I did learn they're a couple 
of worthless layabouts.</i>

04:27.740 --> 04:32.750
<b>Tanabata
Star Festival</b>

04:32.750 --> 04:34.310
<b>July 7th
3PM 5PM 7PM</b>

04:32.750 --> 04:35.980
<b>Concert, Raffle, Fireworks</b>

04:33.310 --> 04:37.750
<b>Orihime</b>

04:33.520 --> 04:35.270
<i>Is this them?</i>

04:34.100 --> 04:37.750
<b>Hikoboshi</b>

04:37.750 --> 04:43.760
<b>Sasamoto Butcher Shop</b>

04:39.030 --> 04:40.660
Why hello, mister.

04:40.660 --> 04:42.750
Care to write one for yourself?

04:45.640 --> 04:46.760
Here.

04:49.870 --> 04:51.990
What do you write on this?

04:52.790 --> 04:56.130
What? Don't tell me you've
 never used a tanzaku before.

04:56.760 --> 04:59.740
You write a wish on it,
then hang it on bamboo.

05:00.650 --> 05:05.650
May I get to
travel a lot

05:00.650 --> 05:05.650
May my dog live 
a long, healthy life

05:00.650 --> 05:05.650
May I become an
 upstanding adult

05:00.650 --> 05:05.650
World peace

05:00.650 --> 05:05.650
<b>May I happen across


a good sauna</b>

05:01.040 --> 05:05.110
You can wish for world peace, 
the well-being of your household... Anything.

05:05.650 --> 05:08.660
<b>May I happen across

a good sauna</b>

05:12.280 --> 05:14.290
What to write...

05:13.710 --> 05:14.810
I know!

05:14.140 --> 05:15.300
<i>My wish?</i>

05:14.290 --> 05:15.300
I'm not sure.

05:15.920 --> 05:18.290
<i>Humanity's downfall.</i>

05:19.080 --> 05:21.870
Here, mister. A croquette on the house.

05:21.870 --> 05:23.590
Fresh from the fryer.

05:25.050 --> 05:28.050
<b>Sasamoto Butcher Shop</b>

05:25.520 --> 05:27.720
Have some fresh croquettes!

05:28.060 --> 05:30.030
Oh, yay!

05:30.550 --> 05:31.810
Thank you.

05:31.810 --> 05:34.280
I hope your wishes come true.

05:34.690 --> 05:35.770
<i>This is good.</i>

05:56.620 --> 05:59.630
<b>Butcher Shop</b>

05:57.030 --> 05:59.150
Two croquettes, please.

05:59.620 --> 06:01.640
Why thank you!

06:01.640 --> 06:03.370
Come back for more, you hear?

06:03.380 --> 06:08.800
World peace

06:03.380 --> 06:08.800
May I pass my exam!

06:03.380 --> 06:08.800
May I get to eat
first-rate yakiniku

06:28.260 --> 06:32.180
May the two of them get to meet

06:43.940 --> 06:44.820
<b>May the world
\hbe at peace

\h\h\h\h-Red</b>

06:44.170 --> 06:45.210
There.

06:44.820 --> 06:46.160
<b>May everyone enjoy
\hgood health

\h\h\h\h-Red</b>

06:46.350 --> 06:47.410
Red.

06:48.260 --> 06:50.300
That's your twelfth one.

06:50.300 --> 06:53.210
How many tanzaku are you going to use up?

06:54.150 --> 06:55.000
I'm on a roll.

06:55.000 --> 06:58.860
Isn't there only one thing
 you should wish for?

06:58.860 --> 07:01.820
"I want a sense of direction."

07:03.390 --> 07:05.070
Sorry I'm like that.

07:05.070 --> 07:06.150
It's okay.

07:06.150 --> 07:07.690
We've just accepted it.

07:08.090 --> 07:11.610
That was all I could think of at first, too.

07:11.950 --> 07:16.450
May Red find his way home
-Blue

07:11.950 --> 07:16.450
May Red acquire a sense of direction
-Blue

07:11.950 --> 07:16.450
May Red stop getting lost
-Blue

07:11.950 --> 07:16.450
Red gets lost so much,
it makes my stomach ache
-Blue

07:11.960 --> 07:15.540
But Blue already wished for it over and over.

07:16.720 --> 07:18.200
Oh.

07:18.450 --> 07:21.610
So I thought I should wish for other things.

07:22.210 --> 07:23.460
<b>Academic
achievement
-Pink</b>

07:23.460 --> 07:24.710
<b>I want some tasty ice cream
-Mugi</b>

07:24.710 --> 07:25.960
<b>I want a tasty crêpe
-Sora</b>

07:25.960 --> 07:27.710
<b>May Pink get 5% 
of my stomachaches
-Blue</b>

07:27.710 --> 07:29.470
<b>May Blue's stomach medicine
 taste ridiculously bitter
-Pink</b>

07:29.670 --> 07:33.140
<b>May everyone be happy
-Red</b>

07:29.770 --> 07:32.300
May everyone be happy.

07:33.360 --> 07:36.200
May conflict cease to exist in the world.

07:33.680 --> 07:36.810
<b>May conflict cease 
to exist in the world
-Red</b>

07:37.180 --> 07:41.310
<b>May those who suffer
from disease find relief
-Red</b>

07:37.360 --> 07:40.790
May those who suffer from 
disease find relief.

07:41.920 --> 07:45.530
May the two of you grow up healthy.

07:48.440 --> 07:53.370
Then we'll write one that says
"May Blue stop having stomachaches."

07:53.370 --> 07:54.870
Yeah, let's do that.

07:54.870 --> 07:56.750
Seriously, I'm really sorry.

07:57.990 --> 08:04.000
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

07:57.990 --> 08:04.000
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

12:26.260 --> 12:27.870
We'll build again!

12:30.590 --> 12:31.900
Yes, we will.

12:32.520 --> 12:35.110
And next time, we'll make them even better.

12:43.950 --> 12:49.950
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

12:43.950 --> 12:49.950
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

12:50.260 --> 12:53.620
<i>I'm Trigger, a higher-up in the Evil League.</i>

13:04.690 --> 13:09.700
<i>I fight day after day here on Earth
in the name of my home planet.</i>

13:11.360 --> 13:15.150
<i>But why must I work with </i>this guy<i>?!</i>

13:17.530 --> 13:20.030
<i>Everyone calls him the General,</i>

13:20.600 --> 13:22.480
<i>and I hate his guts!</i>

13:25.560 --> 13:27.410
<i>What makes </i>him<i> so like a general?</i>

13:28.420 --> 13:32.650
<i>I'll make him see that I'm better than him!</i>

13:35.870 --> 13:39.760
Why do you go home on foot
amongst the Earthlings?!

13:39.760 --> 13:43.220
It's too early in the day 
to go straight home.

13:43.220 --> 13:45.740
Leaping from building 
to building draws attention.

13:45.740 --> 13:48.070
We have warp gates, you know?

13:48.070 --> 13:49.960
They're down for maintenance.

13:52.660 --> 13:56.440
Just my luck. Out on stroll
with you out of uniform.

13:56.980 --> 13:58.190
That's right.

13:58.850 --> 14:03.150
<i>What's with that unkempt hair?</i>

14:03.150 --> 14:05.480
<i>Where did the General go?!</i>

14:06.900 --> 14:09.500
<i>Now he looks a little like 
some kind of mascot.</i>

14:13.340 --> 14:14.370
Hey, look!

14:15.130 --> 14:15.820
What's—

14:16.150 --> 14:17.900
Panda crêpes.

14:17.900 --> 14:18.740
Huh?

14:19.630 --> 14:21.790
Look at that. Panda crêpes.

14:22.930 --> 14:25.050
Okay, and?

14:26.750 --> 14:29.750
Is their cuteness lost on you?

14:29.750 --> 14:33.670
I may not get it,
but don't you look down on me!

14:34.530 --> 14:35.640
Hey!

14:35.640 --> 14:40.150
<b>CRÊPES</b>

14:41.110 --> 14:43.140
One panda crêpe, please.

14:46.610 --> 14:49.430
<i>So the General likes crêpes, huh?</i>

14:49.800 --> 14:52.190
<i>Is the truth that he has a sweet tooth?</i>

14:52.190 --> 14:54.490
<i>How adowable!</i>

14:54.490 --> 14:59.450
<i>If our underlings found out about this,
his image as the General would be ruined.</i>

15:01.280 --> 15:02.610
Trigger.

15:03.210 --> 15:06.260
<b>Panda Crêpes</b>

15:03.480 --> 15:06.260
I can't get a good shot. Hold this.

15:06.260 --> 15:07.320
Huh?

15:13.800 --> 15:15.860
Give me a warning first!

15:15.860 --> 15:19.260
There's the angle! I need to check 
my bangs! I have to be ready!

15:19.790 --> 15:21.350
Don't worry.

15:21.350 --> 15:23.100
Only the crêpe is in frame.

15:23.370 --> 15:25.960
Shut up and eat this already!

15:30.870 --> 15:35.280
<i>What's his deal with the freakin' crêpe?</i>

15:41.480 --> 15:42.990
What're you doing?

15:43.780 --> 15:46.410
I want to eat it, but I feel bad for it.

15:47.340 --> 15:51.000
I can never decide which part to eat first.

16:03.010 --> 16:06.150
Have you been <i>trying</i>
to confuse the heck out of me?!

16:06.550 --> 16:07.830
What's wrong?

16:07.830 --> 16:09.080
You want a crêpe?

16:09.080 --> 16:10.380
No, I don't!

16:10.380 --> 16:14.370
If we're going back to headquarters, 
hurry up and eat the damn thing!

16:14.610 --> 16:15.820
Good call.

16:19.500 --> 16:22.830
<i>A coworker I despise 
has a side I wasn't expecting.</i>

16:22.830 --> 16:24.920
<i>I did </i>not<i> want to know this!</i>

16:26.370 --> 16:29.880
This is the way I like to spend my days off.

16:29.880 --> 16:33.080
If you happen to catch me on one,
don't speak to me.

16:33.080 --> 16:34.260
Huh?

16:34.260 --> 16:37.160
I prefer to enjoy my time off by myself.

16:37.930 --> 16:39.790
Who'd even speak to you anyway?!

16:39.790 --> 16:41.470
Don't be so full of yourself!

16:41.470 --> 16:42.620
Right.

16:56.670 --> 16:58.190
Hey, hey, General.

16:58.190 --> 17:00.950
About those Earth creatures you like...

17:01.490 --> 17:03.230
You mean pandas?

17:03.230 --> 17:04.340
That's them.

17:04.640 --> 17:06.900
It's hard to see their eyes, isn't it?

17:06.900 --> 17:07.900
What?!

17:08.720 --> 17:13.710
When you're not at work,
it's hard to see your eyes, too.

17:14.070 --> 17:15.960
You kinda match the pandas.

17:20.470 --> 17:22.470
<b>Didn't take it as an insult</b>

17:27.490 --> 17:29.420
I <i>will</i> leave on time today!

17:29.420 --> 17:32.950
I bought ice cream at the convenience 
store and got things together for dinner

17:32.950 --> 17:36.230
because there's a special
 panda documentary tonight!

17:36.230 --> 17:38.290
I swear I'm going to watch it live!

17:38.290 --> 17:42.240
I've set it up to record, naturally,
 but that's not the point!

17:44.750 --> 17:46.030
On time, on time, on time.

17:46.030 --> 17:47.590
Panda special, panda special.

17:47.590 --> 17:48.720
On time, on time, on time.

17:48.720 --> 17:50.470
Panda special, panda special.

17:50.470 --> 17:51.770
On time, on time, on time.

17:51.770 --> 17:53.290
Panda special, panda special.

17:53.290 --> 17:54.440
On time, on time, on time.

17:54.440 --> 17:55.250
Panda special...

18:02.210 --> 18:05.070
Are you cheering for me?

18:06.220 --> 18:08.010
Thanks.

18:16.120 --> 18:20.990
<i>In the end, something came up 
today right before quitting time,</i>

18:20.990 --> 18:24.940
<i>and much to my annoyance, 
I had to work very late.</i>

18:25.460 --> 18:28.430
<i>Unfortunately, I have work tomorrow, too.</i>

18:28.430 --> 18:30.820
<i>I need to get to sleep as soon as possible.</i>

18:32.000 --> 18:36.080
<i>But... I can't sleep at all!</i>

18:36.680 --> 18:40.100
<i>My body is clearly in need of rest.</i>

18:40.690 --> 18:43.760
<i>Yet in spite of that,
I find myself wide awake!</i>

18:45.040 --> 18:46.770
<i>I have to sleep.</i>

18:47.700 --> 18:49.390
<i>I have to sleep.</i>

18:50.260 --> 18:52.160
<i>I have to sleep.</i>

18:58.240 --> 18:59.450
<i>It's no use!</i>

18:59.450 --> 19:00.820
<i>Why can't I do it?!</i>

19:01.250 --> 19:03.020
<i>Am I too exhausted?</i>

19:03.020 --> 19:06.540
<i>If I lie here awake too long,
morning will come!</i>

19:06.540 --> 19:09.560
<i>I can't go to work without a wink of sleep!</i>

19:09.560 --> 19:11.700
<i>What a horrifying thought.</i>

19:12.890 --> 19:15.260
<i>The night is so quiet.</i>

19:15.260 --> 19:18.250
<i>It's like being adrift in outer space.</i>

19:20.670 --> 19:24.540
<i>I wonder if those I left behind 
on our world are doing well.</i>

19:25.640 --> 19:30.550
<i>I can't let my brethren experience 
this kind of isolation.</i>

19:31.250 --> 19:36.320
<i>You know, Earthlings talk of counting 
sheep when they can't sleep.</i>

19:36.840 --> 19:40.060
<i>Then I shall count pandas!</i>

19:40.060 --> 19:42.220
One panda.

19:40.070 --> 19:43.910
<b>His ability to think is impaired by fatigue</b>

19:40.070 --> 19:43.910
<b>His ability to think is impaired by fatigue</b>

19:42.220 --> 19:43.900
Two pandas.

19:43.050 --> 19:43.910
<b>His ability to think is impaired by fatigue</b>

19:44.220 --> 19:46.280
Three pandas.

19:46.280 --> 19:47.860
Four pandas.

19:48.270 --> 19:50.110
Five pandas.

19:50.110 --> 19:51.830
Six pandas.

19:51.830 --> 19:53.910
Seven pandas.

19:56.190 --> 19:58.010
Eight pandas.

19:58.010 --> 19:59.770
Nine pandas.

19:59.770 --> 20:01.840
Ten pandas.

20:01.840 --> 20:03.800
Eleven pandas.

20:03.800 --> 20:05.450
Twelve pandas.

20:05.930 --> 20:07.480
Thirteen pandas.

20:18.230 --> 20:20.720
General! What's the matter?

20:20.720 --> 20:23.350
Your face looks even scarier than usual.

20:23.860 --> 20:29.330
I went beyond the number 
of confirmed pandas on Earth.

20:29.330 --> 20:30.910
Say what now?

20:32.730 --> 20:36.750
Earthlings count sheep 
when they can't sleep.

20:36.750 --> 20:38.570
Oh, that.

20:38.570 --> 20:41.780
I hear that's because "sheep" 
and "sleep" sound similar.

20:40.010 --> 20:42.260
*This is just one theory

20:42.260 --> 20:45.260
Then pandas were never going to work.

20:45.640 --> 20:47.500
Go take a nap.

20:47.500 --> 20:49.850
I'll let you use my kotatsu monster.

20:50.590 --> 20:53.420
You've still got that out?

20:53.420 --> 20:55.520
Put away your winter things already.

20:55.850 --> 21:00.770
I mean, I can't argue...
but it's so darn comfortable.

21:04.580 --> 21:05.750
General?

21:07.370 --> 21:10.010
Huh? Did you fall asleep standing up?

21:34.970 --> 21:39.940
<i>In my dream, I gazed at the night 
sky with a hundred pandas.</i>

21:40.920 --> 21:45.530
<i>I told them that shining star was my home.</i>

21:46.420 --> 21:48.030
<i>Or, I think I did.</i>

23:20.000 --> 23:20.710
<b>Mr. Villain's
Day Off</b>

23:21.340 --> 23:25.490
An eternal nap is a momentary illusion.

23:27.380 --> 23:30.420
An invitation from a floral garden.

23:32.900 --> 23:38.140
Beyond the carousel, a maze with no exit.

23:40.060 --> 23:41.940
A bustling circus.

23:43.070 --> 23:45.400
A marvelous trip, like magic.

23:46.140 --> 23:48.640
A pandaful weekend.

23:48.650 --> 23:49.940
A Pandaful Weekend.
